---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Why this exists - Awesome GitHub"
  description="Why the Awesome GitHub site exists and how it supports the conference talk."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Context</div>
    <h1>Why this exists</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The site gives LightSpeed a clean public face for the ideas already living inside
      the <code>.github</code> repository: governance, reusable patterns, the
      conference talk, and the discipline that keeps AI-assisted workflows maintainable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <p>
        It keeps the public site focused on the talk and the standards behind it while
        leaving room for additional pages later.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Shows the repository as a control plane rather than a document dump.</li>
        <li>Gives the conference talk a clear home inside the same public site.</li>
        <li>Keeps the shared header, footer, and page voice consistent across the site.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How it grows</h2>
    <div class="page-copy">
      <p>
        As more conference or project pages are added, they should reuse the same design
        language rather than reset it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
